<spell-notebook "items usage">
	<header level="1">
		Items
		<header>A group of items presents a set of site content for display, each an image beside its
              text.</>
	</>
	<items-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#using-it">Using it</>
			<item link="#events">Events</>
			<item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
			<item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  from the old Astro page (Behaviour, Accessibility), tightened. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			An item here is the same `<ui-item>` that dropdowns, lists and menus use: there is no separate "items item".
			Inside `<ui-items>` it becomes a block with its image on one side and a `<ui-content>` on the other, and it styles
			the content parts inside it (`<ui-header>`, `<ui-meta>`, `<ui-description>`, `<ui-extra>`) as Fomantic's item
			header, meta and so on. The same parts inside a list item still look like list parts.

			- The image: the `image` shorthand, a slotted `<img>` (both at the item's image width), or a `<ui-image size>`
			  (its own size).
			- `link` makes the whole item one link; `appearance="link"` on the group is only the hover look.
			- `<ui-content vertical-align="middle|bottom">` aligns the content against the image;  a
			  `<ui-stack direction="horizontal" justify="end">` in a part (`<ui-extra>`) puts its buttons at the right.
			- Items stack, image above content, below 768px:  of the GROUP's width by default, of the window's with
			  `stack-with="page"` (here, or on a `<ui-root>`);  `unstackable` keeps them side by side. A stacked
			  image takes its natural width, up to 250px tall.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<ui-items divided>
			  <ui-item image="/covers/totoro.jpg">
			    <ui-content>
			      <ui-header link="/films/totoro">My Neighbor Totoro</ui-header>
			      <ui-meta><span>IFC Cinema</span></ui-meta>
			      <ui-description><p>Two sisters move to the country ...</p></ui-description>
			      <ui-extra><ui-label>Limited</ui-label></ui-extra>
			    </ui-content>
			  </ui-item>
			</ui-items>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Events">
		<markdown>
			A group has no events of its own. A link item is a normal link (`click`, then navigation); buttons and links
			inside an item's content fire their native events.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>
			The group is never a tab stop. **Tab** reaches each link item (one stop per item) or the links and buttons inside
			an item's content, in reading order; **Enter** follows a link.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- The group is a `role="list"` and each item a `listitem`, so a screen reader hears how many there are.
			- A link item is one `<a>` whose name is all of its text. Keep other links and buttons out of it, and don't give a
			  linked header its own `link` inside one.
			- Give a `<ui-header>` a `level` when an item's title should be a heading in the page outline.
			- A slotted image needs its own `alt`; the `image` shorthand is decorative (`alt=""`), so put what matters in
			  the text.
			- `disabled` fades the item and sets `aria-disabled`.
			- If the element fails to render, it shows its items through a bare `<slot>`, so they still read in
			  order; the list around them, its spacing and the stacking in a narrow group go.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
